./data/living_catalog_updates/update_2026-08-09/14_snapshot/crop_ledger.json:3135:        "rationale": "The right crop shows the model architecture from H&E imaging through patch/context processing, FiLM, and ST Prediction. This is a direct input-to-model depiction for an actual H2O evaluation route based on histopathology image input. The crop is not just an output or post-hoc analysis.",
./data/living_catalog_updates/update_2026-08-09/14_snapshot/crop_ledger.json:3646:    "selection_rationale": "Figure 2 is the architecture/training schematic and explicitly shows H&E imaging input flowing into the image encoder and contrastive multimodal pipeline. That makes it the clearest candidate for the raw patch-to-model interface for the H2O-ccRCC benchmark route.",
